    "display_name": "Simulating a Viral Post",
    "long_instructions": "In Lesson 7, students complete this exact task: writing a loop that simulates a post going viral over several days, printing each day's view count as it grows, the same \"Day {i}\" print pattern from the syntax you just saw.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n- Complete `simulate` to simulate a viral post over any number of days.\r\n- Ensure that, for each day, `simulate` prints a message in the format: `\"Day {day}: {views} views\"`. Start with day 0.\r\n- Choose the starting conditions for your post and call `simulate`.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip:**\r\n\r\nRemember that Python's for loop can repeat code a certain number of times.\r\n\r\n\r\nFor example:\r\n```python\r\niterations = 10\r\n for i in range(iterations):\r\n    print(i)\r\n```\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nReflection: What might your students find challenging about this task, writing the loop itself, getting the f-string format exactly right, or deciding how views should grow each day?\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Simulate a social media post going viral.",
